Pat reads and posts to the list from beastie, and his login differs
from every other host's. Keeping his configs with the host, rather
than as the shared samples' values, makes beastie's setup explicit:
the ports come from the host's ports list, the hooks from the notmuch
package, and the configs from here.

just install-mail installs them and makes the mail root. The
password goes in a file of its own, readable only by Pat, so the
configs hold no secret and the repo can carry them whole. README.org
documents the setup and the other ways mbsync can take the password.
